    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "HF:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " diuretics for current or previous volume overload, at the lowest dose that stabilizes weight and relieves symptoms; loops first for volume control, then reduce them where possible in favor of an MRA."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "HF starting doses:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " furosemide 20–40 mg PO daily or BID, bumetanide 0.5–1.0 mg daily, torsemide 10–20 mg daily; titrate up to furosemide 120 mg BID by response and renal function; furosemide 40 mg = bumetanide 1 mg = torsemide 20 mg; refractory: IV loop or add metolazone."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Check electrolytes and renal function daily while on IV diuretics, then as needed (especially after a dose increase); doses larger than needed lower cardiac output, worsen renal function, cause hypokalemia and raise mortality."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Interactions (all diuretics):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " lithium—avoid, diuretics cut its clearance and risk toxicity; NSAIDs can blunt the diuretic and antihypertensive effect of loop, K-sparing and thiazide diuretics."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Overdose:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " supportive—replace fluid and electrolyte losses; check electrolytes, carbon dioxide and BP often."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
